# Scatterplots

## ggplot2 Basics {.smaller}

::: {.columns .pv4}
::: {.column width="60%"}
-   The [ggplot2]{.b .blue} package is a part of tidyverse
    -   No need to install or load it separately
    -   It plays nicely with tibbles and wrangling

::: {.fragment .mt1}
-   It implements the [grammar of graphics]{.b .green} in R
    -   The "gg" stands for "grammar of graphics"
    -   Thus, it lets us control all four elements
:::

::: {.fragment .mt1}
-   We will create a [pseudo-pipeline]{.b .green} of commands
    -   However, we will use `+` rather than `|>`
    -   This is because \{ggplot2\} predates the R pipe
:::
:::

::: {.column .tc .pv5 width="40%"}
{{< lif "../../icons/palette.json" trigger=loop delay=5000 colors=secondary:#2a76dd class=rc >}}
:::
:::

## Starting with data


::: {.cell output-location='column'}

```{.r .cell-code}
library(tidyverse)

# CHECKLIST:
# [x] Element 1: data
# [ ] Element 2: mapping
# [ ] Element 3: scales (for free)
# [ ] Element 4: geoms

p <- 
  ggplot(
    data = mpg
  )
p
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](a_Slides_files/figure-revealjs/unnamed-chunk-1-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::


## Adding aesthetic mapping


::: {.cell output-location='column'}

```{.r .cell-code}
# CHECKLIST:
# [x] Element 1: data
# [x] Element 2: mapping
# [x] Element 3: scales (for free)
# [ ] Element 4: geoms

p <- 
  ggplot(
    data = mpg,
    mapping = aes(x = displ, y = hwy)
  )
p
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](a_Slides_files/figure-revealjs/unnamed-chunk-2-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::


## Adding geometric objects


::: {.cell output-location='column'}

```{.r .cell-code}
# CHECKLIST:
# [x] Element 1: data
# [x] Element 2: mapping
# [x] Element 3: scales (for free)
# [x] Element 4: geoms

p <- 
  ggplot(
    data = mpg,
    mapping = aes(x = displ, y = hwy)
  ) +
  geom_point()
p
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](a_Slides_files/figure-revealjs/unnamed-chunk-3-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::


